Private personal coursework (MAT 470, Real Analysis), not a business.

The top-level README already records the deliberate call that this directory
has no VENTURE.yaml: it has no customers, no economics, and no kill criteria,
so there is nothing for the portfolio router to allocate profit-seeking
effort to. This file makes that decision machine-readable so
`portfolio/router/validate.py` skips the directory rather than failing CI on
a missing VENTURE.yaml.

It also carries course textbooks for personal study only, so it should not be
extracted or published if the portfolio is ever split up.

Whether this belongs under `ventures/` at all is still the open structural
question the README flags; this marker does not settle it.
